// WAC Corporal (1945).
// A Tiny Tim solid booster under the WAC Corporal sustainer, the first US sounding rocket.
// Built by hand from plain parts. The shock of the booster's ignition started the
// sustainer, so both light together; the sustainer stands on three rods over the booster
// and fires out between them, and the booster falls away with the rods once it burns out.
// The tank sits above the motor compartment and the instruments ride in the nose.
